spec:
  grid: 11x11, background 0 [observed]
  diamond_frame:
    color: 2 [observed], 1px hollow diamond, radius 3-5
    bbox: spans full grid (side = 2*radius+1 = grid width = grid height)
    pixels: 4*radius cells at Manhattan distance exactly radius from center
  markers:
    placement: on bbox edges, outside the diamond (Manhattan dist > radius from center)
    diagonal_config: one of two opposite-corner pairs (TR+BL or TL+BR chosen randomly)
    coverage: each active edge filled from vertex-adjacent position to the corner, 0-1 gaps allowed per edge
    count: 4-10 total across all active edges
    colors: any non-bg non-frame color (1-9), may repeat, no constraint on uniqueness
    corner_pixel: shared between two adjacent edges, emits rays in both directions
  blockers:
    count: 0-4 interior pixels (Manhattan dist < radius from center)
    color: single color per grid, distinct from all marker colors [observed]
    constraint: each blocker must lie on a ray path of some marker (same row or column)
  transform:
    each marker emits a ray inward perpendicular to its bbox edge
    ray paints bg cells inside diamond with marker color
    ray stops at first non-bg interior pixel (blocker) or exits interior
    frame, markers, and blockers unchanged

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first
  steps:
    1. Pick radius (3-5), set grid to (2r+1)x(2r+1), center=(r,r), draw diamond frame color 2
    2. Choose diagonal config (TR+BL or TL+BR); this determines which half of each edge gets markers
    3. For each active edge half (top, bottom, left, right), fill positions from vertex+1 to corner with random non-bg non-frame colors; optionally omit 0-1 positions for gaps
    4. Optionally place 0-4 blockers inside diamond in a single distinct color; each blocker must share a column with a top/bottom marker or a row with a left/right marker
    5. Run solver to get output; verify no ray conflicts (two markers painting same cell different colors)
    6. Input is the grid before ray painting (already constructed in steps 1-4)
